; The guard: the build gives an error if caravan, caravan.client,
; caravan.websocket or caravan.router depends on unix, on threads or on a world
; of weft. Thus the four libraries run in each world. weft.linux and
; weft.kqueue depend on weft.posix, thus the forbidden weft.posix also forbids
; these two worlds.
; weft.os selects a world of the OS, or no world on another system.
; -linkall links each module of the four libraries, thus a module that no
; other module uses also gets the check. nounix.ml is empty. The windtrap
; suites link unix, thus the guard is a separate executable with no test
; library.

(test
 (name nounix)
 (libraries caravan caravan.client caravan.websocket caravan.router)
 (link_flags (-linkall))
 (forbidden_libraries unix threads.posix weft.posix weft.sim weft.os))
